# Engineering standards

Apply these to all work in this project. They are intentionally generic to every katapult
project; project-specific guidance lives in other rules under `.cursor/rules/` and in
`cursor_context/` (when present).

## Dependencies: always uv

Each subdir (`lib/`, `nbk/`, `api/`, `app/`, `mcp/`) is its **own** uv environment with its
own `pyproject.toml` + `uv.lock`.

- Add/remove dependencies with uv in the relevant subdir, never by hand-editing the lock or
  `pip install`-ing ad hoc:

  ```bash
  cd <subdir> && uv add <package>      # updates pyproject.toml + uv.lock
  cd <subdir> && uv sync               # reconcile the environment
  ```

- Commit both `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`. Keep `requires-python` consistent across
  subdirs. Images bake envs with `uv sync --frozen`, so after dependency changes rebuild
  the container (`.katapult/katx rebuild`) to pick them up.
- Run commands through the env with `uv run` (e.g. `cd lib && uv run pytest`), not a bare
  interpreter.

## Documentation and READMEs: keep them current

Treat docs as part of the change, not an afterthought.

- When you change behavior, an interface, or setup, update the relevant **README** and the
  Quarto docs in the same change.
- Prose/specs/architecture go in `srv/docs/` (Quarto `.qmd`); rerunnable analyses go in
  `nbk/reports/` notebooks. See `katapult-project-conventions.mdc` for the layout and
  `notebook-standards.mdc` for notebook structure.
- `docs/` is **rendered output** - never hand-edit it; regenerate with
  `.katapult/katx render`.
- `kat export-docs <project>` produces a self-contained HTML zip for sharing without a
  server.

## Notebooks: jupytext-paired

Report notebooks under `nbk/` are paired to plain-text percent `.py` via jupytext and are
edited through the `.py`. Full workflow and cell-label scheme: `notebook-standards.mdc`.

## Security

- **Secrets** live only in gitignored env files under `build/` (e.g. credential env_files
  referenced by `docker-compose.yml`). Never commit them, never bake them into the shared
  image, and never write them into `.handoff/`.
- The dev-only MCP service and any `delegate` backend are dev-only; **test/prod images stay
  agent-free** and credential-free.
- Scan before shipping: `kat scan` (Trivy for dependency/secret/misconfig findings +
  Hadolint for the Dockerfile). Rebuild the image after dependency or Dockerfile changes so
  the image scan is current.
- Prefer least-privilege credentials; do not log secret values.

## Tests

- `lib/` carries the test suite: `cd lib && uv run pytest`. Add or update tests alongside
  library changes, and keep the suite green before considering work done.
